{"name":"Fabulous Fawn","hex":"#e5c1a3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fabulous","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to fable, myth or legend.","Characteristic of fables; marvelous, extraordinary, incredible."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fabulous"},{"term":"fawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young deer.","A pale brown colour tinted with yellow, like that of a fawn."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the fawn colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deer","blocks":[{"text":"A deer or true deer is a hoofed ruminant ungulate of the family Cervidae. Cervidae is divided into subfamilies Cervinae and Capreolinae. Male deer of almost all species, as well as female reindeer, grow and shed new antlers each year. These antlers are bony extensions of the skull and are often used for combat between males."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg/330px-Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer","wikidata":"Q23390"},{"title":"Fawn (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Fawn is a light yellowish tan colour. It is usually used in reference to clothing, soft furnishings and bedding, as well as to a dog's coat colour. It occurs in varying shades, ranging between pale tan to pale fawn to dark deer-red.\nThe first recorded use of fawn as a colour name in English was in 1789."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Oola_-_6_months.jpg/330px-Oola_-_6_months.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fawn_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2138972"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/500px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.